ProsperoSunshine: limits on what a request to the GameStream ports may bring

Anyone who reaches TCP 47989 or 47984 (the internet too, once the ports are forwarded) could send a request head of any size,
as Simple-Web-Server's default buffer has no limit, and /pair kept the device name of any length for the five minutes a
pairing waits. Both servers now take at most 64 KiB per request head or body, far above Moonlight's largest request (/pair
with its client certificate in hex, a few KB); a longer head or body ends the connection without an answer. The device name a
pairing request brings is cut to 128 bytes at a UTF-8 character boundary (src/net/exposure.hpp), the length pin() accepts for
the name the operator confirms. An exception other than boost::system::system_error out of a server's handlers (an allocation
failure, say) used to leave its thread and end the process with std::terminate; it is now caught and logged (patch 0032
says what happens then).

--- a/src/nvhttp.cpp
+++ b/src/nvhttp.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #include "globals.h"
 #include "httpcommon.h"
 #include "logging.h"
+#include "net/exposure.hpp"
 #include "net/log_throttle.hpp"
 #include "network.h"
 #include "nvhttp.h"
@@ -54,6 +55,14 @@
 
   crypto::cert_chain_t cert_chain;  ///< Enabled paired-client certificates accepted by Sunshine's GameStream HTTPS server.
 
+  /**
+   * @brief Most bytes a request's head (request line and headers) or body may take on either server.
+   * @details Simple-Web-Server's default is no limit, and anyone who reaches the ports may send. Moonlight's largest request
+   *          is /pair with its client certificate in hex in the query: under 3 KB for its 2048-bit RSA certificate, under 6 KB
+   *          for a 4096-bit one. A longer head ends the connection without an answer, a longer body gets 413.
+   */
+  constexpr std::size_t MAX_REQUEST_SIZE = 64 * 1024;
+
   /**
    * @brief Get the mutex protecting paired-client authorization state.
    *
@@ -1113,7 +1122,9 @@
       fresh_sess.client.uniqueID = unique_id;
